{"duration_api_ms":56403,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"1fe8cfef-4463-4a77-9e3b-e47c60fc17d7","total_cost_usd":1.80647,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":78555,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":4707,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1216},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":78555,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4707,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":78555,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":78555},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-fable-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":4707,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":78555,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.80647,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":1216,"canonicalModel":"claude-fable-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":2,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"schema\":\"agent-ee.decisions/1\",\"candidate_id\":\"7b6d5a949427df9a9100abf2208581f5564cf9ec758e1b0f1fbe731ff3a60283\",\"run_id\":\"a219d556-531c-4bf1-b25a-2f6350cbb45d\",\"decisions\":[{\"finding_id\":\"circuit/geom-probe-assert-noise\",\"disposition\":\"noted\",\"reason\":\"Supported info-level tool-health observation, not a defect. The console log genuinely contains three PROPERTY_ENUM assertion messages despite exit_code 0, but the probe's output was independently confirmed: all five segment blocks in the native board file carry (width 0.25), matching the probe's reported narrowest 0.25 mm and segment count, so the geometry pass against the declared 0.2 mm minimum is electrically and geometrically correct. No declared criterion is violated and no failure mechanism is established for the design itself.\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"work/geometry/console.log\",\"locator\":\"lines 2-4: property.h(607) assert \\\"m_choices.GetCount() > 0\\\" failed in PROPERTY_ENUM()\"},{\"path\":\"work/geometry/execution.json\",\"locator\":\"exit_code: 0\"},{\"path\":\"inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_pcb\",\"locator\":\"segment uuids ae12bf6f, 69a2edc1, 8b528360, a6dab0b4, 7deb1fb0 all (width 0.25)\"},{\"path\":\"work/geometry/geometry.json\",\"locator\":\"tracks[]: five track entries width_mm 0.25; narrowest matches independent read\"}]},{\"finding_id\":\"circuit/gnd-return-single-path\",\"disposition\":\"noted\",\"reason\":\"Canonical ground-redundancy observation; supported and verified, but not a defect. The saved board shows GND connectivity is complete: F.Cu segment 7deb1fb0 joins C1.2 (110.95,100) to the via at (113,100), the via lands in solid B.Cu fill, and the zone's filled_polygon shows thermal spokes reaching J1 pad 3 at (100,105.08); DRC and the geometry probe both report zero unconnected items. No declared criterion constrains ground redundancy, via count, or annular ring, so the single-path topology violates nothing. Retained as a worthwhile info concern for anyone fabricating this fixture.\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_pcb\",\"locator\":\"via (at 113 100) (size 0.6) (drill 0.3) net GND; zone uuid 38a83012 layer B.Cu filled_polygon with thermal spokes around (100,105.08)\"},{\"path\":\"work/drc/drc.json\",\"locator\":\"unconnected_items: []\"},{\"path\":\"work/geometry/geometry.json\",\"locator\":\"unconnected_items: 0; zones[0] filled true net GND\"}]},{\"finding_id\":\"physical/PHY-01\",\"disposition\":\"duplicate\",\"duplicate_of\":\"circuit/gnd-return-single-path\",\"reason\":\"Same condition and mechanism as the surviving canonical finding circuit/gnd-return-single-path: the GND return between C1 and J1 depends on one 0.6/0.3 mm via plus B.Cu zone thermal spokes, with no redundant path. Both findings cite the same via (b71a70d7), zone (38a83012), GND segment (7deb1fb0) and the same zero-unconnected-items evidence; PHY-01 adds only the derived 0.15 mm annular-ring figure. Both are non-defect info concerns, so folding this into the noted canonical finding loses nothing and does not downgrade a defect.\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_pcb\",\"locator\":\"segment uuid 7deb1fb0 net GND; via uuid b71a70d7 size 0.6 drill 0.3; zone uuid 38a83012 thermal_bridge_width 0.5\"},{\"path\":\"work/geometry/geometry.json\",\"locator\":\"tracks[] via entry width_mm 0.6 drill_mm 0.3; zones[0] net GND layers B.Cu\"},{\"path\":\"work/drc/drc.json\",\"locator\":\"unconnected_items: []\"}]},{\"finding_id\":\"physical/PHY-02\",\"disposition\":\"noted\",\"reason\":\"Supported coverage observation, not a defect. The rc-step criterion genuinely declares vout_5ms with no min/max, so the 5 ms measurement is logged but enforces nothing; the check's 'meets all declared measurement limits' summary remains literally accurate because only vout_1ms carries limits, and the fixture requirements bound only the 1 ms point. The measured 0.9932621 V independently matches the analytic 1-exp(-5)=0.99326 V, so no electrical problem exists. Adding a limit would invent a requirement, which adjudication forbids; the finding is preserved as info so the pass is read as verifying one point.\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"work/rc-step/ngspice.log\",\"locator\":\"vout_5ms = 9.932621e-01\"},{\"path\":\"work/rc-step/deck.cir\",\"locator\":\".meas tran vout_5ms FIND v(OUT) AT=5m\"},{\"path\":\"inputs/requirements/fixture-requirements.md\",\"locator\":\"requirement 1: limits apply only to V(/OUT) at t = 1 ms\"}]},{\"finding_id\":\"physical/PHY-03\",\"disposition\":\"noted\",\"reason\":\"Supported scope observation, not a defect. The declared geometry criterion (min_track_width_mm 0.2) covers track segments only, and all five segments pass at 0.25 mm; the via (0.6 mm pad / 0.3 mm drill, 0.15 mm annular ring), zone min_thickness and clearances are governed only by KiCad default DRC rules since the board setup declares no net classes or custom rules. The requirements document itself scopes requirement 2 to track segments and explicitly disclaims manufacturing guarantees, so no declared criterion is violated; the finding correctly cautions that the all-green checks are not fabrication qualification.\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"work/geometry/geometry.json\",\"locator\":\"narrowest_mm 0.25 across 5 segments; via width_mm 0.6 drill_mm 0.3; zones[0].min_thickness_mm 0.25\"},{\"path\":\"inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_pcb\",\"locator\":\"(setup ...) block contains no net classes or custom design rules; via uuid b71a70d7\"},{\"path\":\"inputs/requirements/fixture-requirements.md\",\"locator\":\"requirement 2: 'not an ampacity or manufacturing guarantee'\"}]}]}","structured_output":{"schema":"agent-ee.decisions/1","candidate_id":"7b6d5a949427df9a9100abf2208581f5564cf9ec758e1b0f1fbe731ff3a60283","run_id":"a219d556-531c-4bf1-b25a-2f6350cbb45d","decisions":[{"finding_id":"circuit/geom-probe-assert-noise","disposition":"noted","reason":"Supported info-level tool-health observation, not a defect. The console log genuinely contains three PROPERTY_ENUM assertion messages despite exit_code 0, but the probe's output was independently confirmed: all five segment blocks in the native board file carry (width 0.25), matching the probe's reported narrowest 0.25 mm and segment count, so the geometry pass against the declared 0.2 mm minimum is electrically and geometrically correct. No declared criterion is violated and